    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d598">

                <pb facs="0733" n="613" sameAs="frus:frus1905/pg613"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Japanese
                    Minister.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1905-11-24"><hi rendition="#italic">November 24,
                        1905</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 237.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to your interview with me on
                    yesterday, and acknowledging the receipt of your note of the 23d instant,
                    inclosing copy of the convention of November 17, 1905, between Japan and Korea,
                    by which Japan becomes the medium for conducting the foreign relations of Korea,
                    I have the honor to inform you that I have <pb facs="0734" n="614"
                        xml:id="pg614"/> this day directed by telegraph the withdrawal of the
                    American mission to Korea, and have given instructions that the representation
                    of the United States in diplomatic matters in relation to Korea hereafter be
                    conducted directly with your legation, or through the American legation at
                    Tokyo.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Elihu Root.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
